```
KEY POINTS — WHAT TO REMEMBER FROM ALL W1:

DAY 1 — CLASS & OBJECT:
- class = blueprint, object = real thing
- __init__ runs automatically when object created
- self = this specific object
- self.x = x = permanently store on object

DAY 2 — STATE & VALIDATION:
- state = data that changes over time
- self.balance += amount = update permanently
- always validate before changing state
- return inside method = stop immediately

DAY 3 — INSTANCE METHODS:
- method can call another method: self.average()
- return = sends value back (reusable)
- print = just displays, returns None
- sum(), len(), max(), min() = built-in list functions

DAY 4 — CLASS METHODS:
- class variable = shared by ALL objects
- Employee.total not self.total = correct
- @classmethod takes cls not self
- from_string() = create object from different format

DAY 5 — STATIC METHODS:
- @staticmethod = no self, no cls
- use for validation and calculations
- without decorator = Python crashes auto-passing object
- isalpha() = True only if all letters
```

